---
// Tom Mitchell's definition of machine learning (Machine Learning, McGraw-Hill, 1997),
// typeset as an amsthm-style definition: bold head, italic statement.
---

<section class="panel definition" aria-label="Definition of machine learning, Tom Mitchell, 1997">
  <div class="wrap">
    <blockquote class="def" cite="https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~tom/mlbook.html">
      <p>
        <b class="dh">Definition</b> <span class="src">(Mitchell, 1997).</span>
        <em>
          A computer program is said to learn from experience <i class="v">E</i> with respect to
          some class of tasks <i class="v">T</i> and performance measure <i class="v">P</i>, if its
          performance at tasks in <i class="v">T</i>, as measured by <i class="v">P</i>, improves with
          experience <i class="v">E</i>.
        </em>
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .definition { padding-top: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem); padding-bottom: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem); }
  .def { margin: 0 auto; max-width: 60ch; }
  .def p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--f-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.55rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--chalk-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .dh { color: var(--chalk); font-weight: 700; }
  .src { color: var(--chalk); }
  .def em { font-style: italic; }
  .v { font-style: italic; color: var(--chalk); }
</style>
